{"code":200,"message":"OK","tweet":{"url":"https://x.com/guilleflorvs/status/2113641977388433913","id":"2113641977388433913","text":"Marc Andreessen says the gap between what AI-native startups and incumbents think AI can do is \"the widest he's ever seen.\"\n\nHis exact words: \"The AI-native early stage startups have just a completely different view on what they can do with AI than the typical incumbents in almost any industry.\"\n\nNot slightly different. Completely different.\n\nThat's the actual risk for large companies right now. It's not slow adoption — it's a fundamental miscalibration of what AI is capable of. The startups competing against them haven't made that mistake.\n\nThe asymmetry compounds fast. Incumbents build roadmaps around a floor. Startups build businesses around a ceiling. By the time the floor catches up to the ceiling, the market has already moved.","raw_text":{"text":"Marc Andreessen says the gap between what AI-native startups and incumbents think AI can do is \"the widest he's ever seen.\"\n\nHis exact words: \"The AI-native early stage startups have just a completely different view on what they can do with AI than the typical incumbents in almost any industry.\"\n\nNot slightly different. Completely different.\n\nThat's the actual risk for large companies right now. It's not slow adoption — it's a fundamental miscalibration of what AI is capable of. The startups competing against them haven't made that mistake.\n\nThe asymmetry compounds fast. Incumbents build roadmaps around a floor. Startups build businesses around a ceiling. By the time the floor catches up to the ceiling, the market has already moved.","display_text_range":[0,742],"facets":[{"type":"media","indices":[275,298],"id":"2113641906475270144","display":"pic.x.com/PVOHnTx2k8","original":"https://t.co/PVOHnTx2k8","replacement":"https://x.com/guilleflorvs/status/2113641977388433913/video/1"}]},"author":{"screen_name":"guilleflorvs","url":"https://x.com/guilleflorvs","id":"16